  },
  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A metallic rod of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi></math>&nbsp;is rotated with an angular speed of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#969;</mi></math>&nbsp;normal to a uniform magnetic field <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;about an axis passing through one end of rod as shown in figure. The induced emf will be :</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0046_27b2953e373d.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 242px;\" />.</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#969;</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#969;</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>&#969;</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>L</mi><mi>&#969;</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0046_7c95f44f92fc.png\" style=\"width: 202px; height: 112px;\" /></p><p>Linear velocity at the distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>&nbsp;from the centre can be written as,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>x</mi></math>.</p><p>Therefore, induced EMF due to small element will be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi><mi>&#949;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>v</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>B</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>x</mi></math></p><p>Integrating both sides, we get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8747;</mo><mi>d</mi><mi>&#949;</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8747;</mo><mi>B</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>&#969;</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#949;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>&#969;</mi><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>L</mi></msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>B</mi><mi>&#969;</mi><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p>"
  }
}